    {
      "id": "claim_59380e33cfc84cddba77f17a3475a813",
      "statement": "Migration 0025 revoked all table and sequence privileges (and default privileges for future tables and sequences) from anon and authenticated, so a newly created table is closed until a migration explicitly grants it; RLS decides rows, grants decide table access.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://db/migrations/0025_table_grants.sql#L1-L16",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b47371094ad1ef25bfd7e51c9721182b19dfd24daab09068c18d374de409c23e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6466c4252f8d484caf40b2b2f0a2f4b1",
      "statement": "Migration 0027 enabled RLS on tables existing at that time via a loop, so later tables must enable RLS and add policies themselves; policies wrap app.* calls in (SELECT ...) for once-per-query evaluation. 0047_document_links.sql is a model: enable RLS, grant SELECT, a policy tied to the parent documents row, and the log_catalog_write trigger.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://db/migrations/0027_rls.sql#L1-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f9d4b6e59eb8e9383643292a799830a34b40495022422a439fa9021925f5146:"
        },
        {
