      "id": "claim_aad2169e729a47c7ab9a750d0d0256a1",
      "statement": "At backend boot, the lifespan calls verify_against_db and raises RuntimeError if the SQL catalog lists a table or column absent from the database; extra live tables not in the catalog or KNOWN_EXCLUDED are only logged at INFO and extra columns are not checked, so a new table stays invisible to the agent until deliberately catalogued or excluded.",
